    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of The Environment (Protection) Act, 1986\nObjective To protect and improve the environment and address related matters.\nKey Components\n1.\tDefinitions: - Environment: Encompasses water, air, land, and their inter-relationships.\n•\tEnvironmental Pollutant and Pollution: Defined in relation to harmful substances and their presence.\n•\tHazardous Substance: Substances harmful to humans, living organisms, or the environment.\n2.\tCentral Government Powers: - Regulatory Measures: Setting standards, regulating industries.\n•\tInvestigations and Directions: Power to issue enforceable directions.\n3.\tPollution Control and Abatement: - Emission Regulations: For industries and substances.\n•\tInspections and Sampling: Authorized officers' powers.\n4.\tPenalties and Fund: - Penalties for Contraventions: Including corporate and governmental entities.\n•\tEnvironmental Protection Fund: Established for environmental protection activities.\n5.\tMiscellaneous Provisions: - Good Faith Protection: For actions taken in good faith.\n•\tRule Making Power: With parliamentary oversight.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
